CAT = "nhieReporting"; SEG = "RPT"
Q = [
("Which detail belongs in a report's description of a furnace?",
 "Its fuel type and location", ["Its original purchase price", "The installer's full name", "Its yearly utility cost"],
 "Reports describe each system by its distinguishing features, such as type, energy source and location, so the client knows what was seen."),
("An infrared camera shows a cool spot on a ceiling below a bathroom. The inspector should:",
 "Confirm with a moisture meter", ["Report it as a roof leak", "Report it as missing insulation", "Ignore it as a reflection"],
 "A cool spot can be moisture, missing insulation or air leakage. A moisture meter confirms whether the material is actually wet."),
("A pin-type moisture meter measures moisture in a material by:",
 "Resistance between two pins", ["Surface temperature readings", "Radio frequency density", "Reflected infrared light"],
 "Pin meters drive two pins into the material and read resistance, which drops as moisture rises. Pinless meters use a radio frequency field."),
("When an inspector does not walk on a steep roof, the report should state:",
 "How the roof was viewed", ["That the roof has no defects", "Which roofer to hire", "The roof's exact age"],
 "The report tells the client the method used, such as from a ladder at the eaves, with binoculars or by drone, so the limits are clear."),
("Stored boxes block most of a basement wall on inspection day. The report should:",
 "Note it as a limitation", ["Assume the wall is sound", "Estimate any hidden damage", "Leave the wall out"],
 "What could not be seen is reported, with the reason, so the client knows to look again when the area is cleared."),
("A roof is covered with snow when the inspector arrives. The roof covering should be reported as:",
 "Not inspected, and why", ["In satisfactory condition", "Needing replacement", "Fully inspected from below"],
 "Snow hides the covering, so the report says it was not inspected because of snow and suggests a later look."),
("A standard home inspection is limited mainly to:",
 "Readily accessible, visible items", ["Code compliance of all work", "Concealed wiring in walls", "Systems that are shut down that day"],
 "Home inspection is a visual, non-invasive look at readily accessible systems and components, not a code inspection or a teardown."),
("The gas supply to a furnace is turned off on inspection day. The inspector generally should:",
 "Not operate it and report why", ["Turn on the gas supply", "Relight the pilot light", "Call the furnace defective"],
 "Inspectors do not turn on shut-down utilities or systems. The report says the furnace was not operated and recommends a check once it is on."),
("Which instrument measures carbon monoxide in room air or near an appliance?",
 "A carbon monoxide meter", ["A gas pressure manometer", "A hygrometer", "An infrared thermometer"],
 "A CO meter reads carbon monoxide in parts per million. A manometer reads gas pressure and a hygrometer reads humidity."),
("The home's lights, locks and thermostat are run through the owner's phone app. The report should note that:",
 "App controls were not evaluated", ["The devices are unsafe", "The app's password is weak", "The brand is unreliable"],
 "Smart controls tied to an owner's account are usually beyond the inspection. The report states what was and was not operated."),
("A report gives the location of the main water shutoff mainly so that:",
 "The client can find it fast", ["The lender can approve it", "The appraiser can value it", "Repairs can be scheduled"],
 "Describing where key components are, such as shutoffs and disconnects, helps the client act quickly in an emergency."),
("An inspector views a crawl space only from its access opening. The report should:",
 "Say it was viewed from the opening", ["Describe the space as fully inspected", "Leave the crawl space out", "Recommend replacing the floor"],
 "The method and its limit go in the report so the client knows how much of the crawl space was actually seen."),
("An infrared camera directly detects:",
 "Surface temperature differences", ["Water inside the wall", "Air leaks inside ducts", "Mold growth"],
 "Thermal imaging shows only surface temperature. Moisture, missing insulation or air leaks are conclusions that need other checks."),
("Why should a report state the weather at the time of the inspection?",
 "It affects what could be seen", ["Lenders require it", "It sets the inspection fee", "It dates the home's age"],
 "Rain can reveal leaks, while drought, cold or snow can hide problems or limit what was operated, so conditions are recorded."),
("The data label on a water heater is unreadable. The report should:",
 "Say the age is unknown", ["Guess the age by its looks", "List it as new", "Leave the water heater out"],
 "When the age cannot be confirmed, the report says so rather than guess, and the client can find it from the serial number later."),
("An inspector decides a panel cover cannot be removed safely. The report should:",
 "Say why it was not opened", ["Call the panel safe", "List the panel as defective", "Estimate the wiring age"],
 "Anything not inspected is reported with the reason, such as blocked access or signs of heat, so an electrician can follow up."),
]
